affects grades, and communicate these policies clearly in the course syllabus.\n- **Student
Accountability:** Students are responsible for monitoring their attendance, understanding course-
specific policies, communicating proactively about anticipated absences, and fulfilling all academic
requirements regardless of absence status.\n- **Instructor Discretion within Policy:** Faculty have
authority to define attendance standards, but must apply them consistently, non-discriminatorily,
and in alignment with university-wide guidelines.\n\n---\n\n### 🔹 Commonly Excused Absence
Categories\nUniversities generally recognize the following as valid grounds for excused absences,
which should not result in academic penalties:\n| Category | Typical Requirements
|\n|----------|----------------------|\n| **Religious Observances** | Advance notice (often 1–2
weeks); some schools limit to 2–3 days/year or require verification from a religious official. |\n|
